// PARAM: --analysis interval
// Adapted from Goblint tests/regression/34-localwn_restart/02-hybrid.c
// (Amato-Scozzari, SAS 2013, after Halbwachs-Henry, SAS 2012). Goblint
// proves 0 <= i <= 10 inside the inner loop only with
// solvers.td3.restart.wpoint.enabled (restart.wpoint.once disabled), or
// under the sl4 solver: the inner widening point must be restarted from
// bottom once the outer head narrows.
//
// Voblint answers both bounds UNKNOWN. Mechanism: the inner head is its
// own widening point, and i flows around the inner back-edge unrefined
// (the inner guard j < 10 says nothing about i). The outer head's first
// widening takes i to 2147483647, so i := i + 1 may overflow and delivers
// the full i32 range to the inner head. The outer head later narrows, but
// the inner head's right-hand side joins its value with its own back-edge
// value, so top is a self-fixpoint that narrowing never re-descends
// (measured: i is top at both checks).
// Solver-invariant across join, per-origin, warrow, warrow-per-origin.
fun main() {
  i = 0;
  while (true) {
    i = i + 1;
    j = 0;
    while (j < 10) {
      __voblint_check(i >= 0); // UNKNOWN
      __voblint_check(i <= 10); // UNKNOWN
      j = j + 1;
    }
    if (9 < i) {
      i = 0;
    }
  }
}
